  "live_records": {
    "q-1060": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1060",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
