    "q-73554": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73554",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-8y=10 \\\\  & 3x-7y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
